# Build output
build/
.vs/
out/

# Third-party binaries and anything extracted from them.
# UI-mod art (SkyUI, Untarnished, ...) belongs to its authors -- only the keycap SWFs
# whose terms allow redistribution *with credit* are tracked, and each one ships with
# its credit note beside it. Everything else stays out of the repo; see flash/README.md.
*.swf
!flash/SkyUI/STB_Keycaps.swf
!flash/Untarnished/STB_Keycaps.swf
# The hotbar HUD movie is OURS (tools/build_hud_swf.py builds it from our own slot art,
# and it embeds no icon, keycap, font or SWF of anyone else's), so unlike the UI-mod art
# above it is tracked and shipped. Without it the installer would ship no hotbar at all
# -- package.ps1 could only warn, because CI cannot rebuild it: the source art is local.
!dist/Interface/MMOHotbar/Hotbar.swf
/Skyui/
/Untarnished/
flash/**/build/
flash/**/work/
/package/

# Reverse-engineering scratch: Hex-Rays output of SkyrimSE.exe is Bethesda's code.
/reverse/

# Vendored copy of DIII used as a reference while porting swfhelper.
# The parts actually used live in src/swfhelper/ with attribution.
/Dynamic-Inventory-Icon-Injector/

# Local tooling notes
CLAUDE.md
AGENTS.md

# Local-only asset experiments (user-owned Photoshop/SWF exports, tooling
# scratch). Never part of the build or the FOMOD package.
"/Asset dont push to git/"
/dist/Hotbar.swf.xml
/tools/_out/
/tools/swfdump/
__pycache__/
